- what the story or novel was about
- who wrote it
- explain why it was interesting

I’d like to talk about a novel that I found really interesting, which is Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone by J.K. Rowling. It’s the first book in the Harry Potter series, and it was later adapted into a very successful movie.

I read this novel about three years ago when I was still in high school. At that time, I had just finished watching the movie version and was completely fascinated by the storyline and magical world. Since I wanted to understand the story in more detail, I decided to buy the original novel and read it myself.

The story follows Harry Potter, a young boy who discovers that he is actually a wizard on his eleventh birthday. After receiving a letter from Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry, he enters a completely new world full of magic, friendship, and danger. During his first year at Hogwarts, Harry makes close friends, faces several challenges, and slowly learns the truth about the dark wizard Lord Voldemort, who was responsible for his parents’ death.

What made this novel so interesting to me was the author’s imagination and storytelling ability. The magical world felt incredibly vivid and realistic, and I could easily picture the characters and settings in my mind while reading. Besides that, although the book is considered a fantasy novel for younger readers, it also contains meaningful lessons about friendship, bravery, love, and sacrifice.

To be honest, I enjoyed the book even more than the movie because it included many details and emotions that weren’t fully shown on screen. Overall, it was a really memorable reading experience, and I can totally understand why the Harry Potter series became so popular around the world.
